            <ArticleTitle>Effect of fluvastatin on lipids and fibrinolysis in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study shows that 20-week fluvastatin treatment induces beneficial changes in the lipid panel and a shift in the fibrinolytic pathway toward activation through a decrease in tissue plasminogen activator antigen. Fluvastatin treatment causes no variation in lipoprotein(a) circulating levels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
